    {
      "id": "1578",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 1578,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "Both indicate a basis, but the type of basis differs. を前提に sets a condition or assumption that must hold true, often before action is taken, as in 合意があることを前提に話を進める ('We proceed with the discussion on the assumption that there is agreement.'). をもとに means ‘based on’ and refers to concrete materials, data, or sources actually used to create or decide something, as in 実話をもとに映画が作られた ('The movie was made based on a true story.').",
